input.new_string:
// engine.getHealth()/getStats() are proxied through the single-writer serialize() chain, so
// they queue behind whatever ingest/sync step is CURRENTLY running. /sync is the worst case
// (runIngest's sync_repo branch deliberately runs performSync as ONE giant serialize() slot
// for its whole duration, to avoid a proxy re-entrant-transaction deadlock -- see that call
// site), but a plain /ingest can trip the same failure if a single embed step runs long. Any
// time that queued step outlasts the watchdog's probe timeouts, the client-side call throws;
// -IfUnhealthy's own ingest.running safety check queues behind the SAME chain and times out
// too, so it falls through to "assume wedged" and force-kills a daemon that was actually alive
// and correctly busy (observed 2026-07-01: both an hourly vault-sync and a mem-ingest restarted
// mid-run, each aligned to the watchdog's 5-min-past-:01 tick). Fast path: while ingest.running,
// answer entirely from in-memory state -- never touch the shared chain -- so a busy-but-alive
// daemon reports honestly instead of looking wedged.

